 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "O'er the new moon's golden rim,\nAnd far up aloft above,\nThe stars from silver shimmerings creep,\nLike the dreams of a dreamer's lover.\nAround it, like silver,\nLike glittering silver,\nHis mouth its eyes he kisses softly,\nWhile through the cataract kisses.\nBut never shall I forget\nWhat love did in his kisses,\nOr ever such passionate kisses\nAs these were to me that night. Little",
